00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.629
Speaker 1: We're going to be taking a deep
look at 2024 today.

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:08.720
We're going to look at all sorts of new approval
polls for both the Democratic and Republican

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.720
side.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.600
But before we do that, I have to start with
a story that many of you I know will say,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.950
David, this this can't be this has to be a
low.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.980
Even Fox News, even the right wing wouldn't
do this, would they?

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.680
And yes, they did.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:30.720
Fox News hosts are now worried that the rapidly
declining gas prices that we're seeing might

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.870
be bad for local mom and pop gas stations.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:35.870
I know guys.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:44.409
I know after months and months and months
of saying the high gas prices are the end

00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:46.370
of the of the country.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.929
They are Joe Biden's fault.

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:49.230
It is inflation.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.579
It's ruining everything.

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:56.719
The high gas prices are so terrible now that
gas prices have been declining for about a

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:57.719
month.

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:00.789
And of course, they don't want to give Joe
Biden any credit for it, which, by the way,

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:01.859
I don't think he deserves.

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:03.780
But they were blaming Biden on the way up.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.229
Now they're silent.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:11.299
Now they're saying, you know, these lower
gas prices, they might be bad for gas stations.

00:01:11.299 --> 00:01:12.299
Listen to this.

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:13.450
It is beyond parody.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.729
Speaker 2: I want him to run again and the
rest probably don't.

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:20.280
That is stunning, by the way, on gas prices.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.869
I've had a curious I was at a lacrosse tournament
up in Wilmington, Delaware, over the weekend

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:26.759
in Delaware and northern Maryland.

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:31.500
Regular gas is about anywhere from 455 to
480 a gallon.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.710
So the price is beginning to creep back down.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:34.710
Speaker 3: It is.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.710
It is.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.530
And the point was made over the weekend, I
believe, is The Wall Street Journal.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.710
Gas prices are actually coming back down historically
faster with the price of oil than usual.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:49.840
And it just goes to show you what an incredible
risk reward calculation has to happen on the

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.679
part of those small independently owned, most
of them mom and pop gas stations.

00:01:54.679 --> 00:01:56.100
It's a struggle for all of them.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.729
Speaker 2: They are still a long way from
355 a gallon, but maybe some move in that

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:01.729
direction.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:03.060
Hey, they can't find peace and privacy.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:08.610
Speaker 1: Yeah, no, guys, listen, I mean,
we really have to now think about these mom

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.110
and pop gas stations.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.280
All of a sudden, prices are coming down.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.490
This could really be a bad thing for them.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.450
So we'll ask the question of whether that's
even true.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.840
Just as a reminder, gas prices indeed coming
down.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.910
They peaked right around really about a month
ago, right in mid-June, and have been in a

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.870
relatively steep decline.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.940
I mean, it is true that normally, as I've
as I told you before, there's this phenomenon

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:38.380
where you see oil prices go up and then gas
prices go up in parallel.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:43.100
But then when oil comes back down, the gas
prices only trickle down at a lower rate.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.410
And we've seen this with airfare.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:48.260
We've seen this in a lot of different areas
that are dependent on the oil price.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:54.320
But we're actually seeing a relatively rapid
decline of gas prices now down to about 464,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.070
from a high of about 503.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.330
So it is true that gas prices are coming down.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.810
Now, the question is, is it bad for the mom
and pops?

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:07.100
Is it bad for gas stations when gas prices
are lower, which would imply that it's good

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.830
for gas stations when prices are higher?

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.150
Now, this is not actually even true.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:18.480
And so with all of these discussions, first,
you know, we get the claim from Fox.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.080
First, we want to verify the facts, our gas
prices even coming down.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.250
And yes, they are coming down.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.480
And I reported that to you.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.540
The next question is, do the local gas stations
suffer when prices come down?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.000
It doesn't really work that way.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.080
When when oil prices go up, what you actually
sometimes see is gas stations which make very

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:45.840
little off of gas, try to outcompete competitors
by really eating some of the price increase.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.980
So you will see the gas stations know, okay,
oil prices are up.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.460
The cost we are now paying for gas is up.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.750
So we have to raise our retail price.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:04:00.510
I'm going to try to raise the price less than
my competitor down the street because I make

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:06.970
more money from the slushies and the peanut
magnums and the $10 sunglasses or whatever

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:07.970
else.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.790
So, in fact, sometimes higher gas prices,
higher gas prices are quite good for the oil

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.780
companies, but they are not necessarily so
good for the local gas stations.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:23.130
And during higher prices after expenses, gas
stations will often make only $0.05 a gallon,

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.980
sometimes even less.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:31.820
And that compares to what is often like a
15 to 20 cent per gallon profit for gas stations

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.460
during more stable gas prices.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.130
So multiple aspects of this, the big one is
the hypocrisy.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.040
They've been pulling their hair out with.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.500
The sky is falling type stuff for a year now
about high gas prices, which they say are

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.230
Joe Biden's fault.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.560
We get a month of declines in gas prices now.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.440
They say, oh, no, lower gas prices aren't
so good for the mom and pop gas stations.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.880
What about for all of the commuters that you've
been talking about for a year?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.880
That's the main.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:58.880
Story.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:05.010
The maybe just as interesting one is that
high gas prices are not particularly good

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:09.000
for the mom and pop gas stations for the reasons
that I just said.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:14.890
So it's it's unbelievable that Fox I mean,
they should be embarrassed that now they're

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:19.380
saying gas prices might be going down too
quickly, they might get too low.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.760
It's an embarrassment.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.460
But of course, their followers absolutely
love it.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.940
